===========================================
AWS LAMBDA IMAGE PROCESSOR - COMPLETE SETUP
===========================================

WHAT IT DOES:
Upload image to S3 → Lambda auto triggers →
Creates 5 versions (4k, 1080p, 720p, 480p, 360p)
→ Saves all versions to separate folders

===========================================
STEP 1 - CREATE S3 BUCKET
===========================================
Go to S3 Console
Click Create Bucket
Bucket name     → my-image-processor-2024
Region          → us-east-2
Public access   → Block all (default)
Versioning      → Disable
Encryption      → Default
Click Create Bucket

===========================================
STEP 2 - CREATE LAMBDA FUNCTION
===========================================
Go to Lambda Console
Click Create Function
Option          → Author from scratch
Function name   → image-processor
Runtime         → Python 3.12
Architecture    → x86_64
Execution role  → Create new role with basic Lambda permissions
Click Create Function

After creation:
Click Code tab
Delete existing code
Paste your image processor code
Click Deploy

Click Configuration tab
Click General Configuration → Edit
Memory          → 512MB
Timeout         → 30 seconds
Click Save

===========================================
STEP 3 - IAM ROLE PERMISSIONS
===========================================
Go to IAM Console
Click Roles
Search → image-processor-role
Click Add Permissions → Create Inline Policy
Paste this JSON:

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:GetObject",
        "s3:PutObject"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::my-image-processor-2024/*"
    }
  ]
}

Policy name → image-processor-s3-policy
Click Create Policy

===========================================
STEP 4 - ADD PILLOW LAYER
===========================================
Go to Lambda Console
Open image-processor function
Scroll down to Layers section
Click Edit → Add a Layer
Select → Specify an ARN
Paste this ARN:

arn:aws:lambda:us-east-2:770693421928:layer:Klayers-p312-Pillow:9

Click Verify → Add

NOTE: Do NOT use AWSSDKPandas layer
      That does not have Pillow/PIL
      Use only Klayers-p312-Pillow

===========================================
STEP 5 - ADD S3 TRIGGER
===========================================
Go to Lambda Console
Open image-processor function
Click Add Trigger
Source          → S3
Bucket          → my-image-processor-2024
Event type      → PUT
Prefix          → uploads/
Check the acknowledgement box
Click Add

NOTE: Prefix uploads/ is important
      Prevents infinite loop
      Lambda only triggers on uploads/ folder
      Not on processed output folders

